00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.280
Asaba Barber

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.950
Onii-chan!

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:50.700
What?

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.250
Your boss is on the phone!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.370
My "boss"?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.540
Herro? {<on purpose>}

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.290
<i>Good morning, Correspondent Asaba.</i>

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.300
Club pres?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.380
<i>I think it's about time you executed your mission for today.</i>

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.730
What do you think you're doing?! 
You stupid, perverted idiot!!

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.790
You still need something?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.570
Mom says to hurry up and eat breakfast! {come down for}

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.920
That's all?

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.450
Moron!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.200
What's with her?

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.790
Going somewhere?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.190
Club activity.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.090
Naoyuki, what about breakfast?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:38.880
Don't need it!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.800
I'll be back late tonight.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.130
If you're going out, can you turn on
 the barber pole for me?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:44.720
Okay.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:51.390
Asaba Barber

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.650
Sonohara Station

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:05.990
So sleepy~

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.070
If you fall asleep, 
I'm going to slap you. {punch?}

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.720
Say all you want,
 but I had a really rough night.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.440
I had to predict the location and route of
 their date, and then double-check everything.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:19.250
When was yesterday's Class 3 alert called off?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.920
Around 0500, maybe?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.710
Then when did Kana-chan have time to sleep? {what time did ~ go 2 sleep}

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.550
She's been standing there all morning, 
since 0600? Why didn't you stop her? {still at it}

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.140
Isn't this exactly like the lead-up to the shelter incident?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.640
That's why I dragged you along.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.360
Go right head. If you really think 
she can't handle it, drag her back.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.270
There's still time before Asaba arrives.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.950
Okay... Just one last thing.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.660
Why is Kana-chan wearing
 her school uniform?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.790
School regulations, I'd imagine.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.120
What? No girl heeds{or "pays attention to," but that made the line too long. "obeys" was another option, but that distorts the meaning.} those nowadays.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.000
Maybe she doesn't want to be considered a delinquent?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.420
No way...

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.350
Ah, Kana-chan has a nosebleed...

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.060
Don't worry. Asaba's got
 a handkerchief on him.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.230
All right boys, let's get to it.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.710
Even if we lose them by accident,
you must <i>not</i>  ping Asaba's "bug."

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.520
Iriya will notice it immediately.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.400
Huh?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.500
What's wrong?

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.950
{it seems}Someone's following Asaba.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.620
That girl? {V "wandering daughter, to the west"}

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.830
"Wild Wild Girl, Go West"

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.880
One middle school student...

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.880
One middle school student...

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.680
My, what a coincidence, Asaba-kun.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.600
Roger that.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:02.230
Looks like we were oblivious to a massive conspiracy that was already underway.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.800
Maybe we should've expected this.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.910
He camped out with Asaba on Tonoyama throughout the summer, right?

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.650
Why weren't they removed?

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:11.780
Huh?

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.330
What?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:16.200
You sure know how to crush a boy's dreams...

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.790
Think about it. It was their secret base
 in the back hills.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.330
They spent the entire summer spying on
 the mysterious Sonohara Base,

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.460
stealing watermelons from nearby fields,

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.090
throwing firecrackers into cars where couples were making out,

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:31.160
feeding wild foxes,
 and doing all sorts of fun stuff.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.840
I totally wanted to join them.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.010
Is that what they were up to?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.940
Hey, how much do you know?

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.730
Let's have an information exchange. You first.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.980
Why?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.360
Because it's obvious that 
you know less than I do.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.320
It'll be faster to listen to you first.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:01.290
Onii-chan was acting weird last night. 
After he left, I searched through his room...

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.330
...and found the time and place 
of this movie circled in a magazine.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.710
Who's that girl?

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.670
You came all the way here
 without knowing that?

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.840
She's Iriya Kana, the other person involved in the shelter incident.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.420
That's her?!

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.180
What?

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.100
A live broadcast.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.230
<i>Are you sleepy?</i>

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:27.730
I hid a bug in Correspondent Asaba's bag.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.650
<i>Is the movie boring?</i>

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.740
"Asaba's brother is a pervert{ brother -- this was redundant}!" {this wasn't going to look good without frame-by-frame action to mimic the shaking, therefore I switched it to LazySign.}

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.740
"Look, Look  (Idiot)  Kyaa!   Asaba"

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.420
<i>If you feel tired, go ahead and sleep.</i>

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:57.510
Now! Give her a kiss now,
 Correspondent Asaba!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.000
A kiss for your and our future!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.600
Oh my god! They're all cuddled up together! {how intimate}

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.850
Be quiet. Act like we don't know them.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:14.360
I'm telling you, now's the chance! {make a move}
What are you doing, Correspondent Asaba?!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.160
Look, look at that! This is the first time 
I've seen Kana-chan like that!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.660
Wait, isn't she just asleep?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.250
You think so, too?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:28.110
That aside, why's Asaba still watching the movie?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.590
What's wrong with watching a movie at a movie theater?

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.590
You fool! The movie itself is secondary.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:37.230
Why else would you invite someone to a pitch-dark place like this?

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:41.020
Asaba, go for it! Take this chance to kiss her like you mean it!

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:42.810
You're asking too much of Asaba.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:43.930
Good point.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.440
Ah, she woke up.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:49.770
<i>Kyouko!</i>

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:53.860
What are they saying? Ah, I want to know!

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:54.940
What's that?

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.530
Don't move your head,
 just watch with your eyes.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.570
We've got Suizenji at 10 o'clock.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.240
Is that Yuuko-chan next to him?

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.250
Didn't we get a report of suspicious
 electromagnetic activity around Asaba?

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.630
It's probably Suizenji's work, 
 and a good chance for us to listen in.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:15.010
<i>Oh, yeah... Iriya, you nap a lot
 during classtime, too.</i>

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.550
<i>Are you working part-time or something?</i>

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.260
<i>Does that keep you up late at night?</i>

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.970
<i>Well, it doesn't really matter.</i>

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:25.220
<i>Working part-time is against school rules,
 but a lot of people do it anyway.</i>

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.270
<i>Nobody labels them delinquents.</i>

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.240
We're moving out.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:32.350
But I wanted to listen a little longer...

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.280
Asaba-kun, hand me the bag from that seat.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.700
Get it yourself.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.700
Just do it!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.540
So heavy! What did you put in it?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.680
Things have been strange since last night.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.820
Numerous encrypted transmissions have been circulating in this area.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:53.250
They were heavily scrambled, 
and came from multiple sources.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.800
They stopped around seven this morning,

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.420
but then increased exponentially around ten.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.720
So what?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.890
We may not be the only ones 
observing the two correspondents.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.310
But... ah...

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.280
Don't look!

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:07.810
So, you've noticed them.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.940
Like your brother, you show
 some potential, Asaba Yuuko-kun.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.280
What should I do?

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:16.300
Quit the Theater club 
and join our Newspaper Club.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:18.190
No, that's not what I meant.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.220
If those two are the ones...

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:22.110
I'm going to blast them.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.740
Suizenji changed his seat.
He might be planning something.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.790
Hold on, there's only five minutes left.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.910
Kana-chan just woke up, 
and they started talking again...

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.830
We've stayed too long.
Time to pull out.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:37.820
They're probably using their own
 microphones to tap into my signal.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:41.090
We'll just send out huge amounts
 of interference on the same channel...

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.630
...and blow out their receivers.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.300
So, Asaba-kun. Your mission is to carefully watch all activity in this theater.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.810
So, Asaba-kun. Your mission is to carefully watch all activity in this theater.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.690
What'll <i>you</i>  do?

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:53.520
[ On armband: Sonohara Electromagnetic ]

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:52.440
What else? {isn't it obvious?}

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:55.560
Iriya's Sky

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:55.560
Summer of UFOs

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.650
If you're working, 
you might not have the time...

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.860
The long and the short of it is...

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:09.420
I'd be really happy if you were able to join our Newspaper Club.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.080
What kind of job do you have?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.530
Working at the base.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.460
Would I be able to do it, too?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.920
No, you mustn't!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.000
You really...

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.800
...shouldn't.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.400
W-What was that all about?

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.810
Hey, what's wrong?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.980
W-Wait!

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:51.790
W-What's going on?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.520
Put your hands on the tank!

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:02.420
What did you just throw away?

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.070
Face this way.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.970
W-Wait...

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.600
Take your pants off.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.850
Do it now!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.640
Are they in here?!?

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:17.190
Hey, let go of me! Let go of me, you idiot!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.980
Hey, let go of me! Let go of me, you idiot!

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:21.020
This way!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.360
W-Wait!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.760
Keep a lookout.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.990
Hey, Iriya, what are you doing?!

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.250
Get on.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.110
Hurry up and get on!

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:47.320
What an intricate trap. 
You're fantastic, Correspondent Iriya!

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.050
I wanna go home, 
you dumbass! Let me go!

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.800
NOOO!!!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.770
Iriya! I can't see... in front of me...

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.940
What is up with that girl?

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.110
I wish I knew.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.000
Huh?!

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.210
Correspondent Iriya has an aura of mystery surrounding her.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:11.030
What does <i>that</i>  mean?

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.950
She rides the bus to school every morning.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.790
It starts from the Mitaru Depot, passes by 
Sonohara Base, and ends at Sonohara Station.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.370
What about it?

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:23.380
Until just before summer vacation, there was no such bus.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:33.880
And then there's the phone calls.
She always makes two phone calls every day.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:37.270
It feels like she's listening to 
some kind of information service.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:46.400
There's more. She often gets called to the faculty room by the PA system.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:49.450
In those cases, there's a high probability that she'll leave school early.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.740
Where exactly does she go?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:13.250
Ah, they fell! They fell into the river!
Hey, Iriya!

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:33.200
I seem to be surrounded by a great number of exceptionally talented women.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.640
Oh, <i>really?</i>

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:38.370
And as for Correspondent Asaba,
 from the male faction...

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.730
...there's no way he doesn't know
 more than he lets on.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:52.180
It hasn't been too long
 since the shelter incident.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.970
It's not surprising that 
something would happen.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:58.970
"Asaba's brother is a pervert!"

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.930
No, Onii-chan, you pervert!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:02.020
My brother is..

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.270
Huh?

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.630
My brother is NOT a pervert!!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.030
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.620
I cannot tolerate this any more.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:28.670
Take this! Butterfly kick!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.360
IDIOT!

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:49.650
Hey, it's all right now. Now that we've come this far, we should be fine.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.350
HEY!

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.870
You see, the thing is...

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:05.830
Since we've found one bug,
 I need to examine you thoroughly.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:09.460
There's never just one. 
There has to be more, so...

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.560
A bug?

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.170
You mean that button?

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.390
Ah, a cat.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:26.710
Do you... like cats?

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:32.760
Wait, that was you? You're the one who put a cat in my shoe locker?

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:38.620
Ah, It's not a big deal.
I'm not mad or anything.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:39.530
No!

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:47.020
Do you routinely punch and kick little girls?

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.130
I won't go easy on anyone,
 even if they are women or little girls!

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.210
You monster! Devil! Disgrace to humanity!

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.050
You're the disgrace!

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.200
Why?!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.560
Listen to me.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:03.160
Everyone may say that Correspondent Asaba
took the transfer student into the shelter,

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.270
but the truth is the exact opposite!

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.970
According to eyewitness testimony,

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:12.400
Correspondent Asaba was dragged in there by Correspondent Iriya.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:18.700
That's more logical than the idea that that coward is a wannabe rapist!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.620
My big brother's not a coward! {but he is a wannabe rapist? >do not understand}

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:22.780
Huh?!

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:27.300
So what kind of older brother 
<i>would</i>  you be satisfied with, then?

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.340
I'm going home!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:39.180
What, you can't even offer
 to walk me home?!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:44.210
What?! You little brat!!!

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:58.600
It won't come for another 30 minutes?

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:02.310
Let's wait in here.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.190
Iriya?! What's wrong?

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.180
It's okay... I'm fine...

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:26.850
Riverside Children's Playground
 Sonohara City Kugawa Area 7th Shelter

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.120
You're really fine?

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:27.320
You'll feel better if you sit down.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:33.400
Let's sit over there.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:37.570
Hey...

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.650
I'm really okay now.

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:42.310
But you still don't <i>look</i>  okay. {See my ship? Does it *look* okay to you?}

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:48.350
If you're really feeling bad, 
we can call someone to pick you up.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:55.790
Sorry, I guess you won't tell me about that.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.440
Ah, no!

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.540
I just feel like I asked about 
something inappropriate.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.760
Can you promise me something?

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:10.850
That... you won't tell anyone?

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.600
My comrade died. {fsc}

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:26.700
At the time, there were 
five Manta pilots at Nevada Base...

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.830
Among the five of us, she was the ace.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:33.640
I don't remember who suggested it first, but...

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:37.790
...the remaining four of us decided to go to the crash site.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:41.610
We stole the log from the flight recorder,

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:46.500
and compared its images to satellite photos
 to pinpoint the crash site.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:49.000
Then we snuck out of the base.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:53.760
But eventually, we ran out
 of food and water...

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:56.700
...and thought we might 
wind up dying out there.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.920
That person gave you a ride?

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:16.160
I didn't know what he thought about us. {fsc}

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:22.710
There was a park in the middle of the empty desert. {uninhabited}

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:26.530
In the midst of a desert full of nothingness all the way to the horizon... {fsc}

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:31.470
...it was the only place
 built with concrete and asphalt.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:35.270
There were swings, a jungle gym, see-saws,

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:40.570
and assorted other playground equipment.
The paint still hadn't dried yet.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:44.900
Of course, there wasn't a sign of children anywhere.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.510
There was nobody there except us.

00:21:48.730 --> 00:21:53.300
That was when we felt like 
we were all unwanted kids.

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:58.830
Even while we were alive, we weren't allowed to meet with or talk to anyone else.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:02.570
If we died, we'd be treated as if
 we'd never existed in the first place.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:09.950
Helicopters came and took us back to the base,

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:14.020
but none of us were yelled at. {Ayu: But if no one had come... // wrong} {But nobody scolded us.}

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.580
My story ends here. {Cool story, sis.}

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:22.950
You're the first one I've ever told about this,
so please don't tell anyone else.

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:23.820
Right.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:29.850
Sorry. You went to the trouble of inviting me out,
 but I've been nothing <i>but</i>  trouble.

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:35.160
Why... are you saying this <i>now?</i>

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:33.790
Huh?

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:38.620
{Lunar: Iriya nosebleeding and falling down, that happens every day. // can we say awkward?} {it's normal 4u to get nb and collapse,} Isn't it normal for you to get nosebleeds and pass out?

00:22:58.260 --> 00:22:59.390
Thank you.

